#---
# purpose: "One Enum HOF specialized at three distinct closures keeps its reducer's result type"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# Regression target for fz-f98.17. `Enum.drop_while/2` reaches the recursive
# `List.reduce_while_cont/3`, whose body calls `reducer.(head, acc)` through a
# parameter. The reducer slot arrives from the `Enumerable.reduce_while/3`
# protocol callback, whose spec cannot instantiate it, so the callee type at
# that call is a type VARIABLE (or the real closure joined with one).
#
# The compiler used to read "I cannot resolve this callee" as "this callee is
# dynamic" and earn `any` there. A type variable is not-yet-known, not
# anything-at-all, and the cumulative value-type join never retracts the `any`.
#
# Two distinct closures were green and three were not, so the fixture uses
# three. `x < 0` is false for every element, so `drop_while` drops nothing;
# `x > 0` is true for every element, so it drops everything; `x < 2` stops
# partway. Each closure therefore exercises a different stop point through the
# same shared reducer surface.
fn main() do
  xs = [1, 2, 3]

  dbg(Enum.drop_while(xs, fn (x) -> x < 0 end))
  dbg(Enum.drop_while(xs, fn (x) -> x > 0 end))
  dbg(Enum.drop_while(xs, fn (x) -> x < 2 end))
end
